        ],
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"MindWanderer\"]\n\nI never noticed that the center of Nightmist&#39;s Elder Sign is different from the canonical Lovecraft one. I wonder why Adam changed it.\n\n[/quote]\n\nWell, the canonical Lovecraft one looks like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elder_Sign#/media/File:Elder_sign.jpg\">this</a> as this is how he drew it in a letter (it was never given a detailed description in his stories). The star shaped one is the invention of August Derleth in some of his &quot;posthumous collaborations&quot; with HPL. In one of these he described it as &quot;the rough shape of a star, in the center of which there appeared to be a caricature of a single giant eye; but it was not an eye, rather a broken lozenge in shape with certain lines suggestive of flames or perhaps a solitary pillar of flame&quot; and this is what entered the popular consciousness via games by Chaosium like the <em>Call of Cthulhu</em> RPG and <em>Arkham Horror</em>.\n",
